meta {
  name: list
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?page=1&page_size=20
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.page_info.page: eq 1
  res.body.page_info.page_size: eq 20
}

docs {
  Listing requires the user:list permission, so a member gets 403 here.
  errors/users-forbidden.bru is that same request with a member token.

  A page past the end returns an empty items array with the real total, not
  a 404: asking for page 99999999 is a valid question with a boring answer.

  Query string is written inline in url: only. The Bruno CLI builds the
  request from url: verbatim and reads only path-type entries out of a
  params block, so a params:query block is dropped entirely — not merged,
  and not overridden by a clashing key. Adding a fresh key there would
  disappear just the same. The GUI behaves differently: its params table
  rewrites the URL bar, so the two stay in step there.
}
